From 06038fe0140b047922c7d99720e21c77be622cac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Truong Huy Hoa <huyhoa308@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:09:46 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(dog): real pins, no servos, richer eyes, ToF listen,
 "Chao Nhi" wake word

- Pins match the verified hardware: one full-duplex I2S bus (BCLK 16, WS 17,
  mic DIN 14, PCM5100A DOUT 15) at 16 kHz, mono sent to both DAC slots.
- Servo legs removed (pins 7/4/6/5 held LOW).
- Wi-Fi: power save forced off, Wi-Fi/LWIP buffers in PSRAM and enlarged.
- Eyes: 24 presets, per-mood colour fade, overlays (hearts, tears, blush,
  anger mark, Zzz, ?, !, sparkles, sunglasses, notes, tongue), speaking bob,
  assistant/user text subtitles, idle fidgets and sleepy mode.
- VL53L0X ToF driver (I2C 8/9, XSHUT 21): hand close -> start listening,
  adaptive threshold, stall watchdog.
- Custom MultiNet wake word "chao ni" (Chao Nhi).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
